---
const checks = [
  ['01', 'Buyer launch', 'Confirm how the buyer starts an OCI PunchOut session from their procurement system.'],
  ['02', 'Catalog access', 'Map the buyer connection to the correct Shopify store and accessible catalog.'],
  ['03', 'Cart return', 'Test that selected items return to procurement for the buyer’s approval process.'],
  ['04', 'Downstream order', 'Confirm how the approved PO reaches PunchOut Central so the Shopify order can be created.']
];
---
<main>
  <section class="page-hero page-hero--mint" id="overview"><div class="wrap page-hero__grid">
    <div class="page-hero__copy reveal"><span class="ey">Shopify OCI PunchOut</span><h1>Use OCI PunchOut with your existing Shopify catalog.</h1><p class="lead">PunchOut Central supports OCI-based catalog launch and cart return for configured buyer connections. Shopify remains the supplier storefront, while the buyer’s procurement system handles approval.</p><div class="page-hero__actions"><a class="btn pri" href="/book-demo/">Discuss OCI requirements &rarr;</a><a class="btn secbtn" href="#flow">See the connection &darr;</a></div></div>
    <div class="hero-visual logo-hero reveal"><div class="hero-visual__label"><span>Procurement protocol</span><b>OCI</b></div><div class="logo-hero__mark"><strong>OCI</strong></div><span class="logo-hero__status">PunchOut Central</span><h3>Catalog launch and return</h3><p>Buyer-specific OCI connection to a supplier store.</p></div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="sec" id="flow"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head center reveal"><span class="ey">OCI flow</span><h2>Launch the catalog; return the selection.</h2><p class="lead">OCI connects the buyer’s procurement session to the supplier catalog and returns the selected cart. The approval and PO process follows the buyer’s configuration.</p></div>
    <div class="integration-flow reveal"><div class="integration-node"><strong>Buyer procurement</strong><span>Starts OCI PunchOut</span></div><div class="integration-arrow">&rarr;</div><div class="integration-node integration-node--accent"><strong>PunchOut Central</strong><span>Buyer and session mapping</span></div><div class="integration-arrow">&rarr;</div><div class="integration-node"><strong>Shopify</strong><span>Supplier catalog</span></div></div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="sec soft" id="details"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head reveal"><span class="ey">Connection checklist</span><h2>Test the OCI path with the buyer.</h2><p class="lead">A working catalog launch alone is not the full transaction. Confirm cart return and the downstream purchase-order handoff as well.</p></div>
    <div class="simple-steps">{checks.map(([number, title, description]) => <article class="simple-step reveal"><span class="simple-step__num">{number}</span><h3>{title}</h3><p>{description}</p></article>)}</div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="sec" id="proof"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head reveal"><span class="ey">Order boundary</span><h2>Returning a cart is not placing a Shopify order.</h2><p class="lead">The buyer approves the cart in procurement. When PunchOut Central receives the approved PO, it creates the matching store order and tracks subsequent invoice activity.</p></div>
    <div class="related-grid"><a class="related-card reveal" href="/integrations/procurement-systems/"><span>Buyer side</span><h3>Procurement systems</h3><p>Review buyer-specific connection planning.</p><b>Explore &rarr;</b></a><a class="related-card reveal" href="/integrations/shopify/"><span>Supplier side</span><h3>Shopify integration</h3><p>See how the existing storefront is used.</p><b>Explore &rarr;</b></a><a class="related-card reveal" href="/integrations/cxml/"><span>Another protocol</span><h3>cXML PunchOut</h3><p>Learn about cXML procurement workflows.</p><b>Explore &rarr;</b></a></div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="sec soft" id="faq"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head center reveal"><span class="ey">FAQ</span><h2>OCI questions</h2></div>
    <div class="faq reveal"><div class="fi"><button class="fq" type="button"><span>Does PunchOut Central support OCI?</span><span class="plus">+</span></button><div class="fa"><p>Yes. OCI PunchOut is live: buyer launch, catalog shopping, cart return, approved PO to Shopify order, and invoice activity.</p></div></div><div class="fi"><button class="fq" type="button"><span>Is setup included?</span><span class="plus">+</span></button><div class="fa"><p>Yes. Standard supported integration setup and onboarding are included at no extra charge. Buyer-specific custom development is separate.</p></div></div><div class="fi"><button class="fq" type="button"><span>Is OCI the buyer’s procurement product?</span><span class="plus">+</span></button><div class="fa"><p>No. OCI is a PunchOut protocol used by a buyer procurement environment. The buyer system and its settings still need to be confirmed.</p></div></div><div class="fi"><button class="fq" type="button"><span>Does OCI cart return create a store order?</span><span class="plus">+</span></button><div class="fa"><p>No. It returns the cart for approval. The approved PO is the step that leads to the Shopify order.</p></div></div><div class="fi"><button class="fq" type="button"><span>Can we reuse our Shopify catalog?</span><span class="plus">+</span></button><div class="fa"><p>Yes. PunchOut Central connects the OCI buyer session to the supplier’s existing Shopify or Shopify Plus store.</p></div></div></div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="page-cta"><div class="wrap reveal"><span class="ey">Plan an OCI connection</span><h2>Review the buyer’s launch and cart-return requirements.</h2><p class="lead">We can map the procurement system, supplier catalog and PO handoff together.</p><div class="page-hero__actions"><a class="btn pri" href="/book-demo/">Discuss the connection &rarr;</a><a class="btn secbtn" href="/how-it-works/">See the full workflow</a></div></div></section>
</main>
